.widget_preview/

# Firebase / Cloud Functions
# This is a "bring your own Firebase" app: each user configures their OWN
# Firebase project and their OWN Gemini key, so nobody consumes anyone else's
# quota. The generated client config is therefore NOT committed — run
# `flutterfire configure` to create your own. Only the *.example templates
# (and functions/.env.example) are tracked, to document the shape.
# Real secrets (the Gemini API key) live in functions/.env and are also blocked
# by .githooks/pre-commit as a second line of defence.
lib/firebase_options.dart
android/app/google-services.json
functions/node_modules/
functions/lib/
functions/.env
functions/.env.*
!functions/.env.example
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
firestore-debug.log
